{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The covenant is conditioned on \"concurrent legislation ... having the same effect as this Part\", but nothing defines when legislation has the \"same effect\"; the phrase is a boilerplate recital of mutual assent rather than an operative term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The doubled period in \"Short title..\" is a typographical slip that changes nothing about meaning.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Area of drainage into the Delaware River and its tributaries, including Delaware Bay\" leaves the landward boundary of the basin to hydrology rather than a described line, but the term is workable in practice.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.05},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Compact\" is defined as Part I only, yet the enacted instrument also contains Part II reservations (Section 15.1) that operate on the same subject matter, so the reach of the defined term is not self-evident.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18},
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Net induced adverse effects, whether or not compensated for\" is an open-ended component of \"cost\" with no measuring convention, and \"indirect expenditures\" has no stated boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition of \"facility\" piles specific enumerations onto the catch-all \"or to facilitate any other uses of any of them\" and \"any and all things and appurtenances necessary, useful or convenient\", leaving the reach of the general words against the specifics genuinely uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
   {"issue": "\"Facility\" is a building block of the \"project\" definition in Section 1.2(g), which in turn drives the Section 3.8 approval requirement, so its breadth is contested through those provisions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Any appropriate branch, department, bureau or division thereof, as the case may be\" leaves which federal component is \"appropriate\" undetermined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Project\" is defined by a sprawling sentence whose modifiers are ambiguous: it is unclear whether \"separately planned, financed, or identified by the commission\" qualifies all of the listed works, and whether \"for the conservation, utilization, control, development or management of water resources\" limits the whole definition or only the \"separate facility\" branch.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.88},
   {"issue": "Read with Section 3.8, which subjects to Commission approval any \"project having a substantial effect on the water resources of the basin\", the definition either swallows private activity generally or is confined to Commission-identified works, and the two provisions cannot both be given their natural reading.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Signatory party\" includes the federal government, yet many operative sections speak instead of \"signatory states\" (e.g., Sections 1.6(a), 3.4), so which body a duty falls on varies with the label used.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22},
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Water resources\" is defined to include \"related natural resources\" and \"related uses of land\" without saying what makes a resource or land use \"related\", so the definition's outer edge is indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The finding that \"a single administrative agency is therefore essential\" sits against Section 1.5, which preserves existing offices and agencies, and Sections 11.1(c) and 11.2(c), which keep federal, state and local agency authority intact.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26},
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The declaration that the basin's waters are \"ample to meet all presently projected demands\" points the other way from the operative shortage machinery in Sections 10.2 to 10.4, which assume protected areas and water supply emergencies.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27},
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Equal and uniform treatment to all water users who are similarly situated\" is a purpose statement with no stated test for similar situation, and it is the sort of declared purpose parties invoke to color operative powers.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
   {"issue": "Section 15.1(t) makes the United States' membership contingent on this section surviving constitutional challenge, and Section 15.1(q) reserves Congress's unilateral right to amend, which sits uneasily with the all-party amendment rule of Section 14.20.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"To the fullest extent it finds feasible and advantageous\" makes the Commission the judge of its own directive, so the mandatory \"authorized and directed\" language has no measurable content.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The renewal window \"not later than 20 years nor sooner than 25 years prior to the termination\" inverts the usual order of the limits and reads on its face as an impossible condition until the reader reverses it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Winding up is left to \"such manner as may be provided by act of the Congress\", with no default if Congress never acts and no role for the states that may have triggered termination.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11},
   {"issue": "Section 15.1(d) of Part II provides that the President's member and alternate \"shall serve at the pleasure of the President\", which contradicts this section's \"to serve during the term of office of the President\"; the compact's own endnote acknowledges the two were inconsistent.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.52}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
   {"issue": "The alternate's tenure \"during the term of the member appointing him\" is overridden for the federal alternate by Section 15.1(d), which puts him at the President's pleasure.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": "\"Shall serve without compensation\" is contradicted for the federal member by Section 15.1(r), which permits the President to fix compensation paid by the United States notwithstanding Section 2.4.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"A majority of the membership\" does not say whether the quorum measure is the full five-member body or those present, and Section 14.5(a) shows the drafters knew how to say \"full membership\" when they meant it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Necessary or convenient to effectuate its powers or duties within the basin\" is an elastic test for acting outside the basin, and the consent sentence does not say whether consent is needed for the sale of water outside the basin as well.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.29},
